SQLite
------
contracts/c-abi/redlinedb.h (installed as include/redlinedb.h, with the
include/sqlite3.h shim that includes it) declares a C interface that reuses
the names, constants and function signatures of SQLite's public API so that
programs written for SQLite can build against RedlineDB.
contracts/c-abi/upstream/sqlite-3.53.1/sqlite3.h is an unmodified copy of
SQLite 3.53.1's sqlite3.h, used only by compatibility tests and never
installed. The redline-web server links the SQLite library, built from the
amalgamation bundled in the libsqlite3-sys crate. The SQLite authors have
dedicated SQLite to the public domain (https://sqlite.org/copyright.html);
this attribution is a courtesy, not a licence requirement.

Third-party dependencies
------------------------
Release archives contain third-party Rust crates and, in redline-web, npm
packages, each under its own licence. share/redlinedb/DEPENDENCIES.tsv lists
every one with its declared licence, and share/redlinedb/licenses/ holds the
licence and notice files they ship (share/redlinedb/components/<package>/ in
the redline-web and redline-testing archives).
